  "notable_quotes": [
    "Under AFI zeolite confinement, diffusion is non-monotonic: C6H4Br2 diffuses faster than smaller C6H4BrF despite stronger adsorption and larger size.",
    "Large successive jumps in one direction boost transport for C6H4F2 and C6H4Br2, giving longer trajectories than C6H4BrF in confinement.",
    "C6H4BrF is the slowest in AFI zeolite (0.93×10−8 m2/s), showing the smaller asymmetric molecule can move slower than the larger symmetric one."
  ],
